This guide creates a complete BakingRL package with a visual, a component, a
service, and a connector.

## Prerequisites

- Node.js 20 or newer.
- npm 10 or newer.
- A local BakingRL app checkout if you want to install and test packages in the
  host application.

## Create A Package From npm

Install the published scaffolder:

```sh
npm install -g @bakingrl/create-plugin
```

Create a package:

```sh
create-bakingrl-plugin my-package
cd my-package
npm install
```

Generated packages use the published SDK dependency:

```json
"@bakingrl/plugin-sdk": "^1.0.1"
```

The generated manifest also declares `compatibility.runtimeApi` with the
current runtime API version, `1.0.0`.

## Create A Package From A Local SDK Checkout

When developing this SDK repository itself, install the checkout globally:

```sh
cd BakingRLSDK
npm install
npm install -g . --force
```

Create a package in a sibling plugin repository:

```sh
cd ../BakingRLPlugins
create-bakingrl-plugin my-package
cd my-package
npm install
```

Generated packages use the SDK from the checkout through a `file:` dependency.

After editing SDK types or runtime helpers:

```sh
cd ../BakingRLSDK
npm run build
```

If you changed the generator, package helper, templates, or global command
metadata:

```sh
cd ../BakingRLSDK
npm install -g . --force
```

You can also run the generator without global installation:

```sh
cd BakingRLSDK
npm run create -- ../BakingRLPlugins/my-package
```

## Generated Package Layout

The default template includes:

```txt
bakingrl.plugin.json
package.json
vite.config.ts
src/visuals/scoreboard/index.ts
src/components/team-badge/index.ts
src/components/team-badge/props.schema.json
src/services/match-stats/index.ts
src/services/match-stats/methods.schema.json
src/connectors/twitch/index.ts
scripts/bakingrl-plugin.mjs
```

The manifest declares the runtime capabilities. `vite.config.ts` controls which
source entries are built to the `dist/` paths declared in the manifest.

## Build, Validate, Pack, Install

Use this loop for most plugin work:

```sh
npm run build
npm run check
npm run validate
npm run pack
npm run install:local
```

What each command does:

- `build`: bundles every Vite input to `dist/`.
- `check`: runs TypeScript without emitting files.
- `validate`: verifies manifest shape and built export entries.
- `pack`: writes hashes and creates a `.brlp` bundle in `dist-bundles/`.
- `install:local`: copies the built package into BakingRL's app-data package
  directory.

Local package install directories:

- Linux: `$XDG_DATA_HOME/com.quillianne.bakingrl/packages` or
  `~/.local/share/com.quillianne.bakingrl/packages`
- macOS: `~/Library/Application Support/com.quillianne.bakingrl/packages`
- Windows: `%LOCALAPPDATA%/com.quillianne.bakingrl/packages`

Set `BAKINGRL_PACKAGES_DIR` to override the target during development.

## Test In BakingRL

1. Start BakingRL with `npm run tauri dev` from the app repository.
2. Open the Packages tab.
3. Enable your package.
4. Add visual exports to an overlay layout or custom page.
5. Use the package configuration action if the package declares
   `settings` or `exports.configuration`.
6. Use editor actions to inspect editor-only visual states without launching
   Rocket League.
7. Switch the editor to preview mode when you want the package to use its
   normal runtime path, including services, registry reads, bus events, and
   service RPC.

